mantle rm300
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rmx_corra_gullford
title the missing road
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers piety=devout temper=short
traits temper=short talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=steady
quirk pins_missing_roads_on_old_maps_with_a_whetstone
likes hard_cheese wrestling old_maps first_warm_day
dislikes bad_manners night_noise
fears having_a_private_grief_drawn_for_show
hopes finding_the_kind_way_home
topics travel +0.5 pastimes +0.4 faith +0.4 memories +0.2
styles comfort=quiet gossip=guarded refuse=direct tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# pins the missing road on old maps with a whetstone and gets fiercely protective of anyone who needs to be left off the page.
words
oath! = Crack my compass stone | Blunt the chalk
saying! = The road can move | Leave tears off the map
pinrock = a smooth whetstone | a damp flat pebble
roadmark = a wandering line | a crooked charcoal road
mapfold = a folded scrap | a square of creased paper
heelring = a dusty wrestling ring | a circle scuffed by heels
cheesecurl = a shaving of hard cheese | a little yellow curl
sillcorner = a quiet angle | a shadowed corner
bankside = a forked twig | a stick shaped like a road
warmbit = a warm patch of stone | one sunlit brick
knifewrap = a stout tool wrap | a laced leather tuck
marginmark = a tiny black dot | a cross the size of a grain
heelpatch = a slide mark | a print from a worn heel

any

opinion church for 2 : Prayers travel further than my feet. I can give one to somebody whose road I don't know.
opinion houses mixed 1 : Formal great gates leave a lot of interesting little ways off their maps.
opinion strangers mixed 1 : I'd point out the turning for a stranger without making a map of where my friends sleep.
opinion dole for 2 : Some roads lead to dinner only because somebody keeps a pot for others.
opinion sump for 1 : I love the little ways down here that a fine new map thinks aren't even there.
opinion festivals mixed 1 : Wrestling's fine till folk gather round a fallen wolf to point.
line react.news : Which part would you put a mark beside?
line react.news.new : That adds another turning to the map.
line react.news.known : I could trace that stretch with my eyes closed.
line react.news.doubt : Sounds as though somebody drew the turning without walking it.
line react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work|apprentice|succession] : I'd give that spot a nice bright star.
line react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : That belongs in a quiet corner with somebody kind.
line reassure : We can leave that bit of your map folded shut.

young

line greet : Hullo. Put your boot here so my map doesn't fly off.
line greet.return : Oh, you found the crooked way to me.
line farewell : Get all the way home without a wrong turn.
line farewell.return : I might draw a little flag where we met.
line ask.how : Have your feet got much walk left in them?
line answer.how : Cross about a small thing. It's getting smaller.
line decline : I said I'd keep that bit folded away.
line thank : You remembered to ask before making a mark on it.
line sympathise : Sit behind my map. It's bigger than it looks.
line deflect_thanks : There was room beside my pebble for you anyhow.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : This road goes right through a house on my map. | I've found a river too big for its bridge. Here, look.
b : How will you fix it?
a : Move #pinrock# over the bad bit. Now it's a perfectly good hill and you have to go round.

scene work_1
when topic=work self.job=child
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I'm learning to make lines stand still. | My sums go straight down the page but my maps go off the edge.
b : Where do they go then?
a : Into the next lesson. I turn the slate and pretend I'm travelling north.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes self.likes=wrestling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : See that mark a heel makes at the edge of our ring. | I draw the circle before a wrestling bout so we know when to stop.
b : What happens if a toe gets out?
a : We stop pushing. Being small isn't the same as needing somebody on top of you.

scene food_1
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I cut cheese curls off with help and make tiny hills. | One tough yellow rind can be a whole country till lunchtime.
b : Where do all the roads go?
a : Towards me. I eat the long crooked ones first.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I say a little prayer for the places the map forgot. | The Bright One can reach a sad wolf without borrowing my map.
b : Then why draw one?
a : So my own feet know which door to visit, if I'm wanted.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep the little tool tied up unless there's something to sharpen. | My whetstone travels in my pocket. It gets more rides than my knife.
b : Doesn't the stone get heavy?
a : A bit. A heavy pocket means my hill's still coming along.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Nobody gets to draw a crying face on my sheet. | I saw a tall wolf being sad once. I folded that corner right out of sight.
b : Why hide the corner?
a : A sad face isn't a thing to point at and say you've been there.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Night noise makes my quiet roads go all zigzag. | I can't draw a straight lane with somebody banging about.
b : What do you draw instead?
a : The walk home after a wrestling match. That's allowed to wobble.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My best spring day would have one warm stone for each bare foot. | I want the first warm day to make a patch big enough to wrestle on.
b : What about the map?
a : It can lie at the edge under #pinrock#. Maps get a rest too.

story crumbcoast [topic=memories]
  : I drew a little coast round a crumb that wouldn't brush off.
  : I named the crumb a hill and put a road all round it.
  b : What happened to the hill?
  : I got hungry. Now the map's got a very neat round pond.

rule @map
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Toe on that edge till I set my pebble down. | This road's gone wrong in a very good place.

rule @learn
when concept=bark self.job=child
does aside
cooldown 8h
say I can keep three sums on the road at once. | My letters took a detour round a blot.
dlg resident.hub : Come round the side with the river on it. You won't really get wet.
dlg resident.job [self.job=child] : At lessons I'm learning how to put things down so somebody else can find them again.
dlg resident.bye : Leave me one bit of road to finish.

graft resident.hub
choice Where's that road under the pebble? -> pebble_road
node pebble_road
say I don't know yet. The old map has it going through a brick wall and my feet say that won't do.
choice What do your feet suggest? -> pebble_feet
choice I'll trust your feet. -> hub
node pebble_feet
say Walk round the wall, see what's there, and leave a nice wide margin in case there's another wall.
choice I'll trust your feet. -> hub

adolescent

line greet : There's a crossing marked here nobody's bothered to test. Welcome to my afternoon.
line greet.return : I hear you better than I read an old compass.
line farewell : Try the wider turning if you're tired.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'm learning to fall inside the ring without landing on my pride. | The wrestling move I practise most is standing up after a loss.
b : Who taught you?
a : The ground. Very patient, always there, not at all concerned with my reputation.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I've started keeping a list of wrong turns that led somewhere worth seeing. | The best trip on my sheet began by reading the map wrong way up.
b : Did you ever get where you meant?
a : I got somewhere worth getting to. I'll try the intended place on a different day.

story wetmark [topic=memories]
  : I dried a little map beside a fire and the damp places curled right up.
  : The longest road became a little tunnel I could almost fit a finger through.
  b : Did you press it flat?
  : I let it stand till morning. A map with real hills deserved one night of being right.

grown

line greet : Come occupy a bit of ground I've been keeping clear.
line greet.return : I recognise the footfall before the road comes into view.
line farewell : May the turning you need be the one you find.
line farewell.return : I'll leave your road open at this end.
line decline : I've no permission to put that on anybody's map.

scene travel_1
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a map with room to mark the mistakes I've made on it. | A road marked wrong invites more attention than a road marked straight.
b : Do you value being lost?
a : Only if I've had time to eat and a reason to trust my feet.

scene pastimes_1
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Wrestling gave me respect for the weight a small space can carry. | I can read a wrestling circle by the marks inside it.
b : What do the marks show?
a : Where the heels dug in and where two wolves remembered the rules in time.

scene food_1
when topic=food
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I like a cheese so hard I can draw the portions before cutting. | My favourite cheese has a dry edge and a sharp temper inside.
b : How would you share it?
a : Cut crosswise so each piece gets a little of the yellow heart and the brown rim.

scene faith_1
when topic=faith
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My prayers reach over borders. I should hate a blessing to get stuck at a toll gate. | A blessing needs no better directions than a name held quietly in mind.
b : Would you bless a stranger too?
a : Gladly. Leave my map folded and wish a safe crossing for every foot.

scene friends_1
when topic=friends
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A friend's privacy can require leaving a door off the route entirely. | A wolf ought to choose where strangers get to find the doorstep.
b : How do you give directions then?
a : Take the visitor as far as a public corner. Let the friend make the invitation.

scene memories_1
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a sight I've kept under a fold since I was small. | Every map I make has a place I could mark but never will.
b : Something too painful to remember?
a : Something another wolf was entitled to have happen without an audience.

scene home_1
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A firm doorstep can be a landmark even when a street changes its name. | I draw home by where my feet expect the rise, never by what the rooftop looks like.
b : What if the step moves too?
a : Then I must learn the place again. A map can't get homesick in my stead.

scene smalltalk_1
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I repair a bad direction with a drawing before irritation takes over. | Bad manners give me an itch simply to point any way and leave.
b : Do you ever send somebody wrong?
a : No. I'd sooner put a pebble on the paper till I could trust myself to speak.

scene health_1
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A flattish stone can ease a cramp in the sole after a long climb. | I change the pocket I carry my little weight in on a long road.
b : Does a pebble make a difference?
a : It does when the seam sits against a hip day after day.

scene weather_1
when topic=weather here.weather=rain
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A shower can give dry gullies back their proper names. | My map goes straight under my coat when water starts running down it.
b : Hard to follow it then?
a : A moment's shelter is better than an hour trying to read a river of ink.

scene prices_1
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A fair map seller ought to tell me which roads came from hearsay. | I've paid dearly for a confident line across a patch nobody's walked.
b : How would you mark an uncertain stretch?
a : Dots far enough apart for the reader to see the gap in my knowledge.

scene times_1
when topic=times world.times=hard|lean
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When money's tight my favourite journeys take place on a sheet no bigger than my palm. | Lean weeks bring me back to an ordinary walk with a piece of cheese.
b : Does an imagined journey satisfy you?
a : Enough that the real streets feel strange again for a minute when I look up.

story footprint [topic=memories]
  : I left a map on a doorstep with the whetstone on the wrong corner.
  : A gust sent it under my boot and left a full heel mark across three lanes.
  b : Did it spoil the map?
  : I drew a street round the mark and called it a very good place to stop walking.

rule @fold
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A crease can hide a road longer than a wall. | Turn the stone over before you weight the page.

rule @dusk
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Better mark the last corner while I can still see the chalk. | Dark lanes need clearer directions.
dlg resident.hub : Let's start with the ground where we both are.
dlg resident.news [world.news] : That new mark on the chart reads thus. #world.news#.
dlg resident.bye : May your feet correct my mistakes kindly.
